/*
 * emuh: headless libmgba harness for tools/emu.py (EDS decomp dynamic analysis).
 *
 * Usage: emuh JOBFILE
 *
 * The job file is generated by tools/emu.py; one directive per line, '#' starts a comment.
 * Frame numbers count frames emulated in this job (0 = the boot or the loaded state). Actions
 * scheduled at frame F happen after F frames have run; "keys" for frame F are held while frame F runs.
 * The frame token "end" means after the last frame.
 *
 *   rom PATH                     ROM image to load (required)
 *   sram PATH                    initial SRAM image (read into memory; never written back)
 *   state PATH                   load this savestate before frame 0 (restores SRAM too)
 *   idle ignore|remove|detect    mGBA idle-loop optimisation (default ignore = exact)
 *   frames N                     number of frames to run
 *   keys FIRST LAST MASK         hold MASK (GBA KEYINPUT bit order) for frames FIRST..LAST
 *   shot FRAME PATH              PNG screenshot
 *   dump FRAME ADDR LEN PATH     raw memory dump (bus view, no side effects)
 *   dumpsram FRAME PATH          raw SRAM contents
 *   savestate FRAME PATH         mGBA savestate (includes SRAM)
 *   alias RAM LEN ROM            code at RAM..RAM+LEN is a copy of ROM (map PCs back to ROM)
 *   funcs PATH                   function start addresses (one per line); enables per-instruction probing
 *   trace OUT                    write per-function entry counts (hits, first/last frame, frames active)
 *   tracefrom FRAME              only probe from this frame on (earlier frames run at full speed)
 *   calls OUT                    record (return address, function) call edges
 *   stack                        keep a shadow call stack; watch/break events get a backtrace column
 *   break ADDR                   log every execution of ADDR with registers
 *   breakout PATH / breakmax N   break log path / maximum logged hits (counting continues)
 *   deref REG LEN                with break: also dump LEN bytes at register REG (0..15)
 *   stopat ADDR COUNT            finish the frame in which ADDR executed for the COUNT-th time, then stop
 *   until ADDR SIZE OP VALUE N   stop after the frame in which [ADDR] (SIZE 1/2/4 bytes) OP VALUE becomes true
 *                                for the N-th time (OP is eq or ne; checked at the end of every frame)
 *   settle N                     with stopat/until: release all keys and run N more frames before stopping
 *   watch ADDR LEN r|w|rw        watch memory accesses overlapping ADDR..ADDR+LEN
 *   watchout PATH / watchmax N / watchsum PATH
 *   watchchanges                 log only writes that change the value (counting and the summary see all)
 *   lua PATH                     run an mGBA 0.10 Lua script (callbacks "frame", "keysRead")
 *   luaout DIR                   value of the Lua global OUTDIR
 *   gdb PORT                     run the mGBA GDB stub on 127.0.0.1:PORT instead of the frame loop
 *   info PATH                    write a JSON summary of the run
 */
